  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Establish a written constitution and Bill of Rights guaranteeing civil, social, and economic rights (free healthcare, housing, education, decent work, minimum wage); replace the internal market with an integrated NHS, add funding, reintegrate dentistry, ban tobacco ads, improve nutrition; increase child benefit, restore benefits for 16–17-year-olds, raise pensions, end means testing for residential elderly care, remove utility standing charges for pensioners; free nursery education for all 3–4-year-olds, restore student grants, hire teachers, build up to 20,000 affordable homes and protect new/improved social housing from discounted right-to-buy; adopt the EU Social Chapter, introduce a minimum wage, and a trade union rights charter; increase overseas aid to 0.7% of GDP; emphasize community policing and effective alternatives to prison with a total handgun ban. TEXT_F: Keep public spending under tight control and lower taxes (aim 20p basic, 40p top); oppose EU-level social/employment regulations; expand welfare-to-work and crack down on benefit fraud (inspections, benefit cards, data sharing); expand school selection and grammar schools; extend privatisation/competition (rail, London Underground, NATS, Parcelforce, utilities competition); tougher criminal justice (minimum sentences, end automatic early release, more CCTV, curfews, ID cards); continue Right to Buy; maintain strong armed forces and NATO central; maintain the UK’s constitutional integrity.",
